{"key":"enterprise/T1059.005","id":"T1059.005","name":"Visual Basic","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1059","tactics":["execution"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may abuse Visual Basic (VB) for execution. VB is a programming language created by Microsoft with interoperability with many Windows technologies such as Component Object Model and the Native API through the Windows API. Although tagged as legacy with no planned future evolutions, VB is integrated and supported in the .NET Framework and cross-platform .NET Core. Derivative languages based on VB have also been created, such as Visual…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/005","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--dfd7cc1d-e1d8-4394-a198-97c4cab8aa67","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.722Z","source_object_version":"1.5","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0016","name":"Module Load","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0016","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--c0a4a086-cc20-4e1e-b7cb-29d99dfa3fb1","page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0029","name":"Script Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0029","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9f387817-df83-432a-b56b-a8fb7f71eedd","page":"telemetry/DC0029/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0076","name":"Behavioral Detection of Visual Basic Execution (VBS/VBA/VBScript)","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0076","stix_id":"x-mitre-dete